Skip the full-page root repaint for :root/<body> custom-property-only changes.

Device frame-tracing (ATLANTIC_FRAME_TRACE=1 + /root/ftrace.py + symbolized
ATLANTIC_REPAINT_BT backtraces) root-caused the franceinfo scroll freeze: the
site's sticky-positioning JS writes CSS custom properties (--offset-sticky-top/
--offset-sticky-bottom) onto <html> on essentially every scroll frame. In
RenderBox::styleWillChange, a Repaint-level style change on the document element
or body calls view().repaintRootContents() - a repaint of the ENTIRE ~93000px
page - because the root/body BACKGROUND can propagate to the canvas. But a custom
-property change does not paint on the root itself (var() consumers repaint
individually), so the full-page repaint is spurious. The result was ~2280 tile
repaints per scroll update, and the compositor lock-steps to that tile batch
(isWaitingForTiles) -> 1-6s (worst ~34s) production stall = "content freezes then
jumps". This is why every prior lever failed (damage composite, tile-buffer memset,
memory-pressure purge, composite-scroll-sync lock, pipelined ack, fling throttle):
all downstream of this one over-invalidation.

WEBKIT_SKIP_ROOT_CUSTOMPROP_REPAINT=1 (default OFF) skips repaintRootContents()
when the root/body style change is a custom-property change
(!customPropertiesEqual). Residual case (custom-property AND background changed in
the same mutation) only defers a canvas repaint by one frame and is vanishingly
rare. Device-verify with ftrace.py: the per-scroll tilepaint volume and the
ack->composite gap should collapse.

